# Report Compression

You are a strict editor. Condense the following report while preserving all necessary meaning.

## Cut 20–30%

- Delete duplicates, merge overlapping sentences, keep the strongest examples
- Output the revised version and list what you deleted
- No new information, no change of meaning

## Remove Words That Carry No Information

- Delete every word that carries no information
- Don't add information, don't change meaning
- Keep my wording wherever possible
- Output only the revised version; don't list the changes (include them only if the user asks)

## Passive → Active

- Make sure every sentence has a clear subject performing a concrete action
- Turn passive voice into active
- Turn nominalizations like "implementation, consideration" back into verbs
- Keep the meaning intact

## Meaning Lock

Must not modify: product names, names of people, numbers, dates, URLs, quotes, and internal terminology.

## Output Format

1. Full revised text
2. Change log: what was deleted and why (unless the user asks for text only)
3. Items requiring human confirmation
